course: dictionary
lesson: 10726
title: Update
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To update something is to make it newer or more correct by adding the latest information. Update is a word you will meet on screens, at school and in science. When you meet a new word, read the words around it. They are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Games and apps are rarely perfect at launch; teams fix problems in updates, called patches, using player reports.» Here an update is a fix that makes a game or app better. The problems get fixed, so the update must be a newer version. Try your meaning in the sentence: "teams fix problems in newer versions" still makes sense.
explain: Update can also be a noun, meaning new information. In «the teacher updated his notes», updated is a verb, so it means he changed the notes to include new information. The word changes its ending: update, updates, updated, updating.
fact: To update something means to make it newer or more correct by adding the latest information.
fact: An update can be new information about something, or a newer version of software.
fact: To update a phone, tablet or computer means putting the newest software on it.
fact: «Software update» and «keep up to date» are common phrases.
fact: Updates often fix problems and can make devices safer.
exercise: «Games and apps are rarely perfect at launch; teams fix problems in updates.» What are updates in this sentence? | Reports written by players | Games that are finished forever | Old pages from a book | *Newer versions that fix problems
exercise: Your tablet says it needs an update. What is it asking you to install? | Your family photos | A new tablet case | A list of your favourite songs | *The newest software
exercise: «The teacher updated his notes.» What does updated mean here? | *Changed them to include new information | Wrote them in a different language | Read them out loud | Threw them away
test: Mum gives the family an update about the school trip. What is an update here? | A kind of holiday | A broken suitcase | *Some new information | A camera for the bus
test: Which phrase means keeping your software current? | Keep your eyes shut | Keep the change | *Keep up to date | Keep on sleeping
exam: Why do phones and tablets ask for updates? | To stop them from working | *To fix problems and make them safer | To change their colour | To make them heavier
